dsv41 patch 0065 (21.10.2026): mixed prefill + decode steps of up to 32 tokens (40 with the coop limit raised) as
breakable PIECEWISE CUDA graphs next to the FULL decode graphs. Off: no gain after 0064 (sustained +0.0 %), 446 MiB
less free memory on the head node; not in v19. Base: the v12 files vllm/v1/worker/gpu/cudagraph_utils.py,
model_runner.py, vllm/models/deepseek_v41/attention.py and vllm_exl3_moe/l2pf.py; independent of 0062-0064.
Why: with FULL_DECODE_ONLY (the launcher's default) every step that holds a prefill row runs eagerly. In the profile of
19.10. (4 streams) eager steps of 16-29 tokens on the decode kernels took 224-260 ms, 214-254 ms of it host time, where
a graph round of the same width takes 65-95 ms.
How: upstream's breakable graphs (vllm/compilation/breakable_cudagraph.py) capture the forward in segments and end one
at every eager break: each layer's sparse indexer + MLA (40 a forward) and the Engram prefetch (4). The segments hold
mHC, the projections, KV insert, compressor, indexer Q/K, routed and shared experts, the dense layers and the
all-reduces, and read the step's values from persistent buffers; the breaks read the step's own metadata at replay.
  1. cudagraph_utils.py: PIECEWISE graphs from their own size list (VLLM_DSV41_PW_SIZES, else the capture sizes),
     capped at the plugin's coop limit (VLLM_DSV41_PW_MAX_ROWS, default VLLM_EXL3_MOE_COOP_MAX_TOKENS or 32, at most
     42): above it the plugin captures exl3_moe with fp32 atomics (not reproducible, other rounding than eager). The
     decode graphs keep cudagraph_capture_sizes. Optional PIECEWISE short-context twins (VLLM_DSV41_PW_TWINS), each in
     its own breakable wrapper (a wrapper keys on the token count only).
  2. model_runner.py: the batch's longest sequence also for mixed batches when PIECEWISE twins exist; run_pw_graph gets
     the dispatched bound.
  3. vllm_exl3_moe/l2pf.py: no L2 prefetch in PIECEWISE forwards (a prefetch forked before an attention break and
     joined after it would leave its segment with an unjoined side stream: a capture error).
  4. attention.py: VLLM_DSV41_PW_WIDE=1 breaks at the whole _prepare_and_attn instead (a diagnostic arm).
Rounding: the same kernels as the eager step up to 32 rows; without a twin a captured step scores the indexer where the
eager step takes the short-context branch (same entries in another order). Deterministic run to run.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v17 = v12 + 0064 + 0065 with cudagraph_mode FULL_AND_PIECEWISE,
VLLM_USE_BREAKABLE_CUDAGRAPH=1, VLLM_EXL3_MOE_COOP_MAX_TOKENS=42, VLLM_DSV41_PW_SIZES=8,16,24,32,40 and
VLLM_DSV41_PW_TWINS=512: 10 PIECEWISE graphs next to the 48 FULL ones; kit_bench and arrivals against the production
setup with 0064 running in the same window, decode cells against its stored reference run): kit_bench sustained (4
streams, 90 s) 128.5 -> 128.6 tok/s, concurrent 2 / 4 streams 76.3 / 117.4 -> 76.3 / 116.7; when a short request
arrives next to running streams (~24 / 32 / 40 rows in the mixed step, all on graphs) the running streams lose 20.4 /
46.1 / 65.9 -> 19.1 / 50.0 / 63.3 ms (median) and the new request's first token comes after 219 / 242 / 248 -> 190 /
209 / 216 ms; cost per decode round -0.66 % (geometric mean), tok/s -0.39 %; T=0 texts identical 8/8 and between two
runs; corruption test (30K/100K, 2 each) 0 hits; lowest free memory under load 2,458 -> 2,012 MiB head, 3,535 -> 3,113
MiB worker. With 0064 a mixed step costs the running streams only 20-66 ms (before 0064 and the CPU pin, the profile of
19.10. suggested 150-185 ms per arrival), so little is left for graphs. Not adopted.
Switch: cudagraph_mode FULL_AND_PIECEWISE (the launcher's GRAPH) with breakable graphs; VLLM_DSV41_PW_SIZES,
VLLM_DSV41_PW_MAX_ROWS, VLLM_DSV41_PW_TWINS, VLLM_DSV41_PW_WIDE. With FULL_DECODE_ONLY every switch is inert.

